      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think we can get rid of this (and [the mocking](https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/4506542/comment/29a73347_49ab0f12/)) if we change `fill_encrypted_private_key` and `encrypt_data_in_place` to take the TPM seed as an argument (or actually `ikm`). That will require refactoring the existing code. One way to do that would be to create two functions for `derive_encryption_key`.\n\nSomething like:\n\n* `get_ikm_and_derive_encryption_key`\n* `derive_encryption_key`\n\nwhere `get_ikm_and_derive_encryption_key` just calls `derive_encryption_key` after calling `get_ikm`. Existing code would be changed to call `get_ikm_and_derive_encryption_key` and these new functions could just call `derive_encryption_key`.",
