      "side": 1,
      "message": "The problem is not only the ikm, but also the user_id.\n\nPassing too many function parameters will decrease the readability of the code, and it\u0027s error prone style that the caller may accidentally pass parameters with the wrong order.\n\nIdeally, nothing should stay in the global scope, we should only pass class references \u0026 call member functions. But that is not the way we do under the EC framework now.\n\nDoing a large scale refactoring should be another project.",
